@startuml
title Appendix — Bayesian Beta-binomial review-elevation signal
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth 220

rectangle "Customer activities" as input
rectangle "Transparent binary mapping\nELEVATED if:\nstatus != completed\nOR CRYPTO\nOR PAYMENT receiver != CH" as mapping
rectangle "Observed counts\nn activities\nk elevated" as counts
rectangle "Prior\np ~ Beta(1,4)\nmean = 0.20" as prior
rectangle "Conjugate update\np | data ~ Beta(1+k, 4+n-k)" as posterior
rectangle "Reference question\nP(p > 0.40 | data)" as threshold
rectangle "RiskSignalEvidence\nposterior-review-elevation-rate\nscore in [0,1] + provenance" as output

input --> mapping
mapping --> counts
counts --> posterior
prior --> posterior
posterior --> threshold
threshold --> output

note bottom of posterior
Worked example:
1 elevated / 1 observation
raw ratio = 100%
posterior = Beta(2,4)
posterior mean ~= 33.3%
P(p > 0.40) = 0.33696
end note

note bottom of output
Derived Stage-1 evidence only.
Synthetic heuristic, not production AML calibration.
Source risk facts remain unchanged.
end note
@enduml
